Package: fletchR
Type: Package
Title: Makes better Arrow files for single-cell multi-assay chromatin analysis
Description: ArchR is great for single-cell chromatin analysis, but its design, 
             interactive tools for exploratory analyses, and kooky file formats
             leave a bit to be desired. iSEE is fantastic for exploration and 
             spitballing; when combined with igvR (igv.js running on a socket),
             plotting genomic abundance, factor loadings, chromatin states, etc.
             becomes more intuitive. fletchR bolts these components onto fast
             Arrow (parquet) out-of-memory operations and expands the machinery
             to handle assays where a single DNA fragment can carry information
             about multiple different assays (proteins, chromatin modifications,
             transcription, DNA methylation, etc.) and jointly model the result.
